WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.241
[MUSIC]

00:00:04.241 --> 00:00:08.698
Director's Consortium is an executive
program for directors of public companies

00:00:08.698 --> 00:00:11.830
or people who serve on boards
that are likely to go public.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:16.390
This program emerged as a collaboration
between the business school and

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:17.630
the law school.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:22.570
Drawing on both the expertise that our
faculty have around the many facets

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:24.280
of being successful in business.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:29.970
And the legal foundation of the role of a
director and their legal responsibilities.

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.350
&gt;&gt; I bought probably 50
companies have been bought,

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:35.662
myself 10 times pretty much
thought I knew everything.

00:00:35.662 --> 00:00:40.360
And then going through the process and
realized, well, I don't know everything,

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:43.590
just seeing how other directors
deal with similar situations.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:46.960
&gt;&gt; As board directors, you get yourself
in big trouble when you stop learning and

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.810
when you start thinking
that you know a lot.

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:51.710
You do, but you don't know it all.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:55.320
&gt;&gt; There are two distinctive features
to the Directors Consortium.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.340
The classroom setting which allows for

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:01.420
intensive interaction among
the faculty and the participants.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:04.160
And the second is the grounding
of the program and

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:07.370
research which provides
directors with frameworks and

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:11.550
evidence to address the questions
that they face in the boardroom.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.127
&gt;&gt; The faculty here is very engaging.

00:01:13.127 --> 00:01:17.637
They teach in a manner that you are not
just thinking about what they are teaching

00:01:17.637 --> 00:01:20.360
but also reflecting upon your experiences.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:22.810
They have a way to elicit conversation.

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:24.940
&gt;&gt; We've tried to keep the cohort small,

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:29.370
because we expect that the learning
doesn't happen only from the experts and

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:33.250
them sharing what they're
seeing on the research front.

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:35.340
But also in a collaborative fashion.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:39.520
&gt;&gt; This provides a good forum for
us to kind of let our hair down and say,

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:41.650
this is my situation,
that's your situation.

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:44.700
&gt;&gt; All perspectives come
together to give each participant

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:48.700
a really rich understanding
of the new ones.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:53.960
&gt;&gt; The content aims to provide
fundamentals and foundations, but also to

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:59.010
keep the board members abreast of all of
the emerging issues facing corporations.

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:03.670
Cutting edge issues like cybersecurity,
challenges facing the audit committee,

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:07.910
how to manage risk, how an official and
intelligence is going to play a role.

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:11.640
And what that means for directors and
the boards they serve on.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:16.200
&gt;&gt; The option modules relate to
basic principles of accounting and

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.440
basic principles of finance.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:22.120
This is for board members who might
feel rusty about these topics,

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:25.758
as well as board members who might not
be as well versed with these topics.

00:02:25.758 --> 00:02:28.060
&gt;&gt; These are rules of thumb.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:32.990
These are tool kits that will
be applicable not just today but

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:37.370
years from today and
they apply across every board.

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:41.580
&gt;&gt; I'm going to go by with lots of
ideas for best practices of how we can

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:46.470
run the board by even being in veteran
leader myself and my current job.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:48.060
&gt;&gt; Without a doubt it was worth coming.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:51.960
Without a doubt I've enhanced
my skill set, my being good.

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:57.256
&gt;&gt; When I think about the boards that I
sit on and what I brought to those boards

00:02:57.256 --> 00:03:02.640
before this course, and what I will
bring to the boards after this course,

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.990
really shows that there
is a lot to be learned.

